===Etymology 1===
Borrowed in the early 18th century from {{bor|ru|de|Kubus}} or directly from {{bor|ru|la|cubus}}, from {{der|ru|grc|κύβος||[[die]], [[cube]]}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|c,a|adj=куби́ческий}}

# {{lb|ru|geometry}} [[cube]] {{gloss|shape with six square sides}}
# {{lb|ru|mathematics}} [[cube]] {{gloss|number raised to the third power}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[два]] [[в]] '''ку́бе'''|2<sup>3</sup>}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} [[cubic meter]] ([[cubic metre]])
#: {{uxi|ru|[[пять]] '''кубо́в''' [[бетон|бето́на]]|five '''cubic meters''' of concrete}}

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table|c,a}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ru|кубату́ра}}
* {{l|ru|ку́бик}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|bg|куб|bor=1}}
* {{desc|kk|куб|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sah|куб|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|ru|orv|кубъ||[[drinking]] [[vessel]]}}, {{etydate|14th century|nocap=1}}, further origin uncertain.

Cognate with {{cog|uk|куб||[[wooden]] [[dish]]}}, {{cog|pl|kubek||[[bowl]], [[cup]]}}, {{cog|dsb|kub||[[bowl]], [[cup]]}}, also {{m|dsb|kubk}}.

Per Vasmer, likely related to {{noncog|sa|कुम्भ|t=[[pot]]}}, {{noncog|ae|𐬑𐬎𐬨𐬠𐬀|t=[[pot]]}}, {{noncog|grc|κύμβος||[[vessel]]}}, {{m|grc|κύβη||[[cup]]}}, also {{m|grc|κύμβη}}.

However Trubachev notes that there are no signs of a nasal vowel and reconstructs {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*kubъ}}, thus rejecting a possible link to {{noncog|ine-pro|*kumbʰo-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kumbʰéh₂-||vessel}} and proposing a connection to {{m|ine-pro||*koubʰ-}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|c,a|adj=ку́бовый}}

# [[boiler]], [[still]], large [[tank]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[перего́нный]] '''куб'''|[[distillation]] '''boiler'''}}

